From a4a756f6fa0b7ca379ae2584355706e2ca3f99c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 13:55:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 009/638] third_party/libxml: select the generated
 AROS-compatible config [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: libxml had no target_os=aros branch, so GN selected no generated platform configuration for the cross build.

FIX_REASON: Reuse the portable configuration family already selected by Linux-class targets; this changes configuration data only and does not claim Linux kernel semantics.

SCOPE: third_party/libxml/BUILD.gn OS include selection.

VALIDATION: the headless_shell graph generated and compiled downstream XML consumers before reaching the Skia platform layer.

RISK: low; one AROS-only GN condition.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 third_party/libxml/BUILD.gn | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/libxml/BUILD.gn b/third_party/libxml/BUILD.gn
index 1621a21578..f51f4cfc74 100644
--- a/third_party/libxml/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/libxml/BUILD.gn
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 
 # Define an "os_include" variable that points at the OS-specific generated
 # headers.  These were generated by running the configure script offline.
-if (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android || is_nacl || is_fuchsia) {
+if (is_linux || is_aros || is_chromeos || is_android || is_nacl || is_fuchsia) {
   os_include = "linux"
 } else if (is_apple) {
   os_include = "mac"
